<section class="page-hero page-hero-compact">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Privacy</p>
    <h1>What stays<br><em>where.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      The short version: reminder data lives on your phone first, the coding
      workspace and its keys stay on the phone, and this website stores only the
      account, snapshot and identity rows needed for the dashboard and bot.
    </p>
    <p class="page-meta">Last updated 21 November 2026 · developer preview</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell prose">
    <h2>The Android app</h2>
    <p>
      Ei Void stores reminders, repositories, chats, settings and usage counters
      in the app's private storage on your phone. Provider keys and the GitHub
      token are encrypted with the Android Keystore. Ei Void does not run an
      analytics SDK and does not send telemetry to us.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you ask the agent to work, the context it needs is sent to the AI
      provider you configured. Git operations go to GitHub. Sign-in and the
      GitHub connection are handled by Clerk. Those services have their own
      privacy terms; Ei Void does not proxy their traffic.
    </p>

    <h2>Reminders</h2>
    <p>
      A reminder is scheduled on the phone. When you sync, the app sends a
      snapshot to this website: title, merchant, bank, amount, currency, due and
      notification timestamps, repeat rule, category, notes, paid and active
      flags, plus your timezone and notification hour. The website uses that
      snapshot to answer <span class="mono">/usage</span>-style bot queries and to
      show the dashboard. It is not a bank feed and has no credentials.
    </p>

    <h2>The coding agent</h2>
    <p>
      Repository contents, prompts and provider keys do not reach this website.
      The one credential the website relays is the GitHub OAuth token you already
      connected through Clerk: the app asks this service for it with a Clerk
      session, and the service asks Clerk's Backend API. The token is returned to
      the authenticated app and is not logged or stored by the website.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses first-party cookies: a signed form-integrity cookie
      (<span class="mono">eivoid_form</span>, up to 30 days) and a CSRF cookie
      (<span class="mono">eivoid_csrf</span>, up to 1 hour). They are HttpOnly and
      SameSite=Lax, and Secure in production. Clerk also sets the cookies its
      own sign-in widget needs. There is no advertising or analytics cookie.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th><th>Where</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Clerk user id and email</td><td>Identify the account</td><td>Postgres account row</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Reminder snapshot</td><td>Bot answers and dashboard summary</td><td>Postgres reminders</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Discord id and username</td><td>Link the companion account</td><td>Postgres account row</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Plan and usage counters</td><td>Show the dashboard and bot usage</td><td>Postgres snapshots</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Device key digest</td><td>Authenticate usage uploads</td><td>Postgres, SHA-256 only</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Waitlist email</td><td>One note when the preview is ready</td><td>Postgres waitlist</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Link codes</td><td>Single-use Discord confirmation</td><td>Postgres, expire in 10 minutes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Request logs</td><td>Operate and secure the host</td><td>Render's platform logs</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on Render and uses a Render Postgres database. Render
      processes ordinary request metadata such as IP addresses and user agents
      as part of operating the service. Secrets — the Clerk secret key, mail
      credentials, the database URL and the Discord bot token — stay in the
      server environment and are never rendered or sent to a browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Discord</h2>
    <p>
      When you run <span class="mono">/link</span>, the bot receives your Discord
      user id and username. The link code is single-use and expires after ten
      minutes. Bot replies are ephemeral. The bot does not request the Message
      Content intent and does not read your messages.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting data</h2>
    <p>
      The dashboard has a <strong>Delete website data</strong> button. It removes
      the account row and, by cascade, the reminder snapshot, usage snapshots,
      device keys and Discord link. Signing out clears the website cookies. App
      data is removed by clearing the app's storage or uninstalling it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children and changes</h2>
    <p>
      Ei Void is a developer tool and is not directed at children. If the preview
      changes its data practices, this page will be updated before the change
      takes effect.
    </p>

